    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > output.txt << 'EOF'\nRemote work has really stuck around since the pandemic. What started as an emergency measure became something a lot of people actually prefer. The flexibility is the biggest win—being able to work from home, a coffee shop, or while traveling has changed how many of us approach our careers.\n\nVideo calls, project management apps, and messaging tools have made it possible to stay connected with teammates regardless of where everyone is. Sure, it's not perfect for every job or every person, but for those who've made it work, the trade-off between office time and personal freedom has been worth it.\n\nThis isn't going anywhere. Companies and workers are still figuring out what works best, but remote work has proven it can be sustainable long-term.\nEOF\\n",
